10
00:51:36,000 --> 00:51:42,000
She Said is a 2022 American drama film directed by Maria Schrader and written by Rebecca
Lenkiewicz, based on the 2019 book by reporters Jodi Kantor and Megan Twohey.

11
00:56:45,600 --> 00:56:51,600
The film stars Carey Mulligan and Zoe Kazan as Twohey and Kantor, respectively, and follows their New York Times
investigation that exposed Harvey Weinstein's history of abuse and sexual misconduct against women.

12
01:01:55,200 --> 01:02:01,200
The film also stars Patricia Clarkson, Jennifer Ehle, Samantha Morton, and
Andre Braugher, in his final film role before his death in 2023.

13
01:07:04,800 --> 01:07:10,800
Ashley Judd appears as herself.

14
01:12:14,400 --> 01:12:20,400
The book was optioned in 2018, and the film was announced in 2021 as a
co-production between Annapurna Pictures and Plan B Entertainment.

15
01:17:24,000 --> 01:17:30,000
Filming took place in New York with cinematographer Natasha Braier.

16
01:22:33,600 --> 01:22:39,600
During post-production, editing was completed by Hansjörg
Weißbrich and the score was composed by Nicholas Britell.

17
01:27:43,200 --> 01:27:49,200
She Said had its world premiere at the 60th New York Film Festival on October 13, 2022, and
was released in the United States on November 18, 2022, by Universal Pictures.

18
01:32:52,800 --> 01:32:58,800
The film received generally positive reviews from critics, who praised
the screenplay and the performances of Kazan and Mulligan.

19
01:38:02,400 --> 01:38:08,400
It was also named one of the best films of 2022 by the American Film Institute.

20
01:43:12,000 --> 01:43:18,000
However, it was a box-office bomb, grossing $13.9 million
against a production budget of $32 million.

21
01:48:21,600 --> 01:48:27,600
The film was nominated for Best Actress in a Supporting Role for Mulligan and Best
Adapted Screenplay for Lenkiewicz at the 76th British Academy Film Awards.

22
01:53:31,200 --> 01:53:37,200
It also earned Mulligan a Golden Globe Award nomination and
Lenkiewicz a Critics' Choice Award nomination.

23
01:58:40,800 --> 01:58:46,800
The film explores themes of based on novel or book, journalism,
biography, sexual violence, sexual harassment.

24
02:03:50,400 --> 02:03:56,400
The tone is emotional.
